post-it: Stops before Windows starts
cause: Bad RAM module
symptoms:
	Stops before Windows starts
	Error text at startup
	Restarts by itself
	Blue screen
	No picture at all
checks:
	yes: Memory test fails at startup
		shows: "Memory test fail", then "System halted"
	no: Windows starts
hardware steps:
	Remove the computer shell
	Swap one RAM module for a new one from storage
	Switch it on: if the memory test passes, the module that you took out was bad
	If the test still fails, put that module back and swap the other one
	Throw the bad module in the trash
	Remount the shell
notes:
	Nothing on the modules shows which one is bad: the player finds it by swapping one and switching the computer on.
